.TH GIT-CA 1 "2026-09-10" "git-ca 0.2.6" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
git-ca \- draft git commit messages and pull request text with GitHub Copilot or OpenAI Codex
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B git ca
.RI [ OPTIONS ]
.RI [ COMMAND ]
.br
.B git-ca
.RI [ OPTIONS ]
.RI [ COMMAND ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B git-ca
is a Git subcommand that drafts commit messages and pull request text using
either GitHub Copilot or the OpenAI Codex (ChatGPT) backend. For commits it
reads the staged diff, asks the active backend for a Conventional Commits
message, writes the draft to Git's commit message file, and runs
.BR git-commit (1).
For pull requests it summarizes branch changes, asks the active backend for a
title and Markdown body, and runs
.BR gh-pr-create (1)
or
.BR gh-pr-edit (1)
(if an open pull request already exists).
.PP
Git handles
.B git ca \--help
by opening this manual page. For clap-generated command help, use
.B git ca \-h
or
.BR "git-ca \--help" .
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-n , " \--no-verify"
Skip pre-commit and commit-msg hooks.
.TP
.BI "\-m, \--model " MODEL
Use a specific model id for drafting. The id must be valid for the active
account's backend. Overrides the persisted default model.
.TP
.BR \-y , " \--yes"
Accept generated text without opening the editor. For commits, this commits
directly. For pull requests, this creates or updates the pull request directly.
.TP
.BI "\--rules-file " PATH
Replace only writing rules with a UTF-8 file for this invocation. Fixed
Conventional Commits instructions and the PR role and JSON contract remain.
Custom rules replace default rules; include any writing safeguards to retain,
such as not inventing test results or issue references.
The explicit file bypasses local Git rules-config lookup and default-file
reads without persisting a setting. This global option has no short alias and
works before or after
.BR pr ,
with either source, for PR creation and updates. Auth, models, and config
commands accept but ignore it.
.PP
Rules files are read once; valid contents are preserved verbatim.
Relative flag paths resolve from the invocation's working directory, including
repository subdirectories; absolute paths work directly. Any extension is
accepted. No tilde expansion, interpolation, or stdin syntax applies;
.B \-
is a literal filename.
Missing, unreadable, directory, non-UTF-8, empty, or whitespace-only explicit
files cause exit 1 with a path and reason, without contents or fallback,
before generation, editor review, commits, or PR creation/updates.
.PP
Without the flag, read repository-local
.B ca.rulesFile
using Git's local config lookup. Global/system settings are ignored; the last
local value wins. One configured file applies to commits and PR creation or
updates with either source. Auth, models, and config never look it up.
Set with
.B git config \--local ca.rulesFile prompts/rules.md
and remove with
.BR "git config \--local \--unset-all ca.rulesFile" .
.PP
Precedence: explicit flag, local setting, command-specific default, built-in rules.
Relative configured paths resolve from the current work-tree root, including
subdirectory invocation and linked worktrees; absolute paths work directly.
Spaces and literal path text are preserved, with the same UTF-8 file rules
as the flag. Configured paths bypass default-file reads. Empty or whitespace-only
settings, invalid configured files, and Git lookup failures cause exit 1
without fallback, generation, editor review, commits, or PR mutation.
Diagnostics identify ca.rulesFile and the path and reason where applicable,
without printing file contents.
Repository, configuration, and source preconditions may fail first.
.TP
.BR \-h , " \--help"
Print command help when the binary is invoked directly or through
.BR "git ca \-h" .
.TP
.BR \-V , " \--version"
Print version information.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.BI "auth login [\--provider " PROVIDER "] [" ACCOUNT "]"
Log in via the chosen backend's OAuth flow. PROVIDER is
.B copilot
(GitHub device flow) or
.B codex
(ChatGPT OAuth via PKCE with a localhost callback on :1455 / :1457). When
.BI \--provider
is omitted on an interactive terminal,
.B auth login
prompts for a choice; when stdin is not a TTY (CI, piped input) it defaults
to
.BR copilot .
When ACCOUNT is provided, store credentials for that named account and make
it active.
.TP
.BI "auth set-token [--account " ACCOUNT "] " TOKEN
Store a GitHub token manually for a Copilot account and make it active.
The Codex backend is OAuth-only and not supported here. If ACCOUNT is not
provided, the token is stored under the default account.
.TP
.BI "auth use " ACCOUNT
Select the named account; the backend is determined by which provider that
account was logged in with.
.TP
.BI "auth logout [" ACCOUNT "]"
Delete locally stored tokens. When ACCOUNT is provided, only that named account
is removed.
.TP
.B auth status
Show local auth state, the active account's provider, all linked accounts, and
provider-specific token state (Copilot token TTL or ChatGPT account/last
refresh).
.TP
.B models
List available models from the active account's live backend catalog.
Codex shows listed models in server priority order.
Codex discovery requires the Codex CLI on PATH and uses its installed version
to query the catalog.
.TP
.BI "pr [\--base " BRANCH "] [\--source " diff|commits "]"
Draft a pull request title and Markdown body for the current branch, then run
.BR "gh pr create"
(or
.BR "gh pr edit"
if an open pull request already exists).
When
.BI \--base
is omitted, the base branch is resolved from
.BR origin/HEAD ,
falling back to
.BR main .
The default source is the branch diff against the merge base; use
.B \--source commits
to summarize commit messages instead.
Use
.B \--yes
on this command to skip editor review and create or update the pull request directly.
Persisted PR auto-accept config has the same effect.
.TP
.B config list
Print all persisted config values.
.TP
.BI "config set-model " MODEL
Persist the default model. For Copilot accounts the id is validated against
the live model list; for Codex it is accepted verbatim because the backend
has no listing endpoint.
.TP
.B config get-model
Print the persisted default model, if any.
.TP
.BI "config set-auto-accept " true|false
Persist whether generated commit messages commit without opening the editor.
This setting does not apply to pull request creation.
.TP
.B config get-auto-accept
Print the persisted commit auto-accept setting.
.TP
.BI "config set-auto-accept-pr " true|false
Persist whether generated pull requests are created without opening the editor.
.TP
.B config get-auto-accept-pr
Print the persisted PR auto-accept setting.
.SH EXAMPLES
.TP
Draft a commit message and open the editor:
.B git ca
.TP
Draft with a specific model:
.B git ca \-m gpt-4o
.TP
Draft with invocation-specific commit rules:
.B git ca \--rules-file ./prompts/commit.md
.TP
Draft with invocation-specific PR rules:
.B git ca pr \--rules-file ./prompts/pr.md
.TP
Place the global option before the PR command:
.B git ca \--rules-file ./prompts/pr.md pr
.TP
Draft from commit messages with custom PR rules:
.B git ca pr \--source commits \--rules-file ./prompts/pr.md
.TP
Commit the generated message directly:
.B git ca \--yes
.TP
Draft a pull request against develop:
.B git ca pr \--base develop
.TP
Create or update the generated pull request directly:
.B git ca pr \--yes
.TP
Show clap-generated help instead of this manual page:
.B git ca \-h
.SH FILES
When XDG_CONFIG_HOME is non-empty, the config directory is
.IR $XDG_CONFIG_HOME/git-ca ;
otherwise it is
.IR ~/.config/git-ca .
Without
.B \--rules-file
and local
.BR ca.rulesFile ,
each drafting command reads only its own default rules file.
Missing defaults silently use built-in rules; empty or unreadable defaults
(including invalid UTF-8) warn and use built-in rules.
.TP
.I ~/.config/git-ca/config.json
User preferences, including default model and commit/PR auto-accept behavior.
.TP
.I ~/.config/git-ca/auth.json
Local credential cache. Each account is tagged with its provider; Copilot
accounts hold a GitHub token plus a cached Copilot API token, Codex accounts
hold ChatGPT access/refresh/id tokens and the linked account id.
.TP
.I ~/.config/git-ca/commit-system-prompt.md
Optional manually edited rules-section override for commit message drafts.
.TP
.I ~/.config/git-ca/pr-system-prompt.md
Optional manually edited rules-section override for pull request drafts. The
built-in JSON response contract stays in the prompt.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR git (1),
.BR git-commit (1),
.BR gh (1)
